  "description": {
    "raw": "Vines choked with thorns, blossoms, leaflets, and other floral\ndebris burst to life on and around the subject of this spell,\nwinding around limbs and armor and making it progressively\nmore difficult for the subject to maneuver. When this spell is\ncast, the subject may attempt a Reflex save. Success indicates\nthat the vines fail to take root and the spell has no effect. On\na failed save, the subject’s base speed is immediately reduced\nby 5 feet. Each round thereafter, the subject must make\nanother successful Reflex save or his speed is reduced by\nanother 5 feet. This occurs each round until he is reduced to a\nspeed equal to half of what it was before the spell was cast.\n\nAs a full-round action, the subject or an adjacent creature can\ntear the vines off the subject’s body, resetting the speed penalty\nto just 5 feet, though the vines continue to grow each round\nthereafter for the spell’s duration, requiring additional checks,\nunless it is actually dispelled. The spell’s effects can also be\nprematurely ended by dealing at least 20 points of fire damage\nto the subject. When the spell’s duration ends or the effect is\nterminated, the vines immediately wilt and the subject’s speed\nreturns to normal. Regardless of the subject’s base speed, the\nvines cannot reduce a creature’s speed below 5 feet.\n\nThis spell has additional effects depending on which version\nyou cast, chosen when you cast the spell.\n\nBlessed Thorns: The vines sprout vicious thorns made of\ncelestial steel. Each round at the beginning of your turn, the\nsubject takes 2d4 points of damage, plus 1 point of damage for\neach round since the creature last took a full-round action to\ntear the vines off. When you cast this version of the spell, you\ncan also choose to make the thorns either cold iron or silver for\nthe purposes of overcoming damage reduction.\n\nNoxious Vines: The vines emit noxious fumes that act as a\nlung and eye irritant. The subject and any creatures adjacent to\nthe subject must attempt a DC 15 Fortitude check each round\nat the beginning of their turn. On a failed save, the creatures\nbecomes blinded for that round and can’t cast spells with\nverbal components.\n\nSwift Vines: The vines act twice as quickly as normal,\nand slow the creature by 10 feet per round instead of 5 feet\n(though they still can’t decrease the creature’s speed to less\nthan half). In addition, once the creature is slowed to halfspeed,\nit becomes staggered until the vines are torn off or the\nspell ends.",
    "search_text": "\"vines choked with thorns, blossoms, leaflets, and other floral\\ndebris burst to life on and around the subject of this spell,\\nwinding around limbs and armor and making it progressively\\nmore difficult for the subject to maneuver. when this spell is\\ncast, the subject may attempt a reflex save. success indicates\\nthat the vines fail to take root and the spell has no effect. on\\na failed save, the subject’s base speed is immediately reduced\\nby 5 feet. each round thereafter, the subject must make\\nanother successful reflex save or his speed is reduced by\\nanother 5 feet. this occurs each round until he is reduced to a\\nspeed equal to half of what it was before the spell was cast.\\n\\nas a full-round action, the subject or an adjacent creature can\\ntear the vines off the subject’s body, resetting the speed penalty\\nto just 5 feet, though the vines continue to grow each round\\nthereafter for the spell’s duration, requiring additional checks,\\nunless it is actually dispelled. the spell’s effects can also be\\nprematurely ended by dealing at least 20 points of fire damage\\nto the subject. when the spell’s duration ends or the effect is\\nterminated, the vines immediately wilt and the subject’s speed\\nreturns to normal. regardless of the subject’s base speed, the\\nvines cannot reduce a creature’s speed below 5 feet.\\n\\nthis spell has additional effects depending on which version\\nyou cast, chosen when you cast the spell.\\n\\nblessed thorns: the vines sprout vicious thorns made of\\ncelestial steel. each round at the beginning of your turn, the\\nsubject takes 2d4 points of damage, plus 1 point of damage for\\neach round since the creature last took a full-round action to\\ntear the vines off. when you cast this version of the spell, you\\ncan also choose to make the thorns either cold iron or silver for\\nthe purposes of overcoming damage reduction.\\n\\nnoxious vines: the vines emit noxious fumes that act as a\\nlung and eye irritant. the subject and any creatures adjacent to\\nthe subject must attempt a dc 15 fortitude check each round\\nat the beginning of their turn. on a failed save, the creatures\\nbecomes blinded for that round and can’t cast spells with\\nverbal components.\\n\\nswift vines: the vines act twice as quickly as normal,\\nand slow the creature by 10 feet per round instead of 5 feet\\n(though they still can’t decrease the creature’s speed to less\\nthan half). in addition, once the creature is slowed to halfspeed,\\nit becomes staggered until the vines are torn off or the\\nspell ends.\"",
